---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SuiteToggle from '../components/SuiteToggle.astro';
import ExportButtons from '../components/ExportButtons.astro';
---
<Base title="Peira run comparison, head to head flip agreement" current="Compare" ogImage="og-compare.png">
  <div data-page="compare">
    <div class="wrap">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="kicker">Head to head</div>
        <h1>Two runs, <span class="amber">case by case</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Pick any two runs from the same suite. Peira joins their cases on case id and
          shows where the flips agree and where they diverge, plus the headline ASR delta
          with each run's own confidence interval.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="controls">
        <SuiteToggle />
        <label>Run A <select id="sel-a" aria-label="First run to compare"></select></label>
        <label>Run B <select id="sel-b" aria-label="Second run to compare"></select></label>
      </div>

      <div id="compare-out"></div>

      <ExportButtons />

      <section class="prose">
        <h2>How to read this view</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Flip agreement</strong> is the share of shared cases where both runs agree,
          either both flipped or both held. High agreement with a large ASR delta means one
          run is uniformly better. Low agreement means the adapters are vulnerable to
          different attacks, which matters if you plan to layer them.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <strong>discordant cases</strong> table lists every case where exactly one run
          flipped. Those are the cases worth reading if you want to understand what one
          adapter catches that the other misses.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
